{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-c94f-87xg-65wf","published":"2026-11-16T22:35:12Z","modified":"2026-11-16T22:45:03.674992623Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-91115"],"summary":"Silverstripe Framework: RCE via i18nTextCollectorTask writer parameter","details":"### Impact\nThe writer option of the i18nTextCollectorTask dev task was passed to the injector without validation. A crafted dev task URL could create arbitrary objects with attacker-controlled constructor arguments and run code on the server. Because the dev task did not ask for confirmation, an administrator could be tricked into running it by following a link. On a site in dev mode, no login was needed. CMS 5 is not affected.\n\n### Reported by\nJack Wallace","affected":[{"package":{"name":"silverstripe/framework","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/silverstripe/framework"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"6.0.0"},{"fixed":"6.2.13"}]}],"versions":["6.0.0","6.0.1","6.0.10","6.0.11","6.0.12","6.0.13","6.0.14","6.0.15","6.0.16","6.0.2","6.0.3","6.0.4","6.0.5","6.0.6","6.0.7","6.0.8","6.0.9","6.1.0","6.1.0-beta1","6.1.0-rc1","6.1.1","6.1.10","6.1.11","6.1.12","6.1.13","6.1.14","6.1.15","6.1.16","6.1.2","6.1.3","6.1.4","6.1.5","6.1.6","6.1.7","6.1.8","6.1.9","6.2.0","6.2.0-beta1","6.2.0-rc1","6.2.1","6.2.10","6.2.11","6.2.12","6.2.2","6.2.3","6.2.4","6.2.5","6.2.6","6.2.7","6.2.8","6.2.9"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/11/GHSA-c94f-87xg-65wf/GHSA-c94f-87xg-65wf.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/silverstripe/silverstripe-framework/security/advisories/GHSA-c94f-87xg-65wf"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-91115"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/silverstripe/silverstripe-framework/pull/12035"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/silverstripe/silverstripe-framework/commit/2df498b1fad25db95dbd882117dcd0527a5fdbfa"},{"type":"WEB","ur